    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d170">

                <pb facs="0325" n="311" xml:id="pg311"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.20/7–1449: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Embassy in the United
                        Kingdom </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-07-15T20:00:00-04:00">July 15, 1949—8 p.
                            m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2476. Dept fully concurs recommendation your 2754, July 14 (532 to Paris) that
                    you should approach Bevin after Senate has completed action on Pact re obtaining
                    agreement for US observers to attend mtgs Permanent Commission. Agreeable that
                    observer be Executive Director ECC when appointed. In actual operation this will
                    have to be handled so as not to give cause to non-WU Atlantic Pact countries for
                    suspicion that we are minimizing their interest by concentration on WU
                    activities. Believe this can be satisfactorily handled by relationship
                    established between Executive Director of ECC, our Ambassadors and
                    representatives of such countries.</p>
                <p>Department concurs your paragraph 3 that at an appropriate time you should raise
                    question of your sitting with Consultative Council when discussing matters of
                    interest to US. Department agreeable to leaving timing to you.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
